Subject: [PATCH] net: preserve internal sockets with Android network restrictions

Creating a network namespace from an unprivileged user namespace invokes
IGMP setup in that task's context. The Android group check rejects its
kernel-owned control socket with EACCES, which IGMP reports as ENOMEM.
Apply this check to userspace sockets only, as the raw-socket capability
check already does. Keep ordinary IPv4/IPv6 socket restrictions intact.

--- a/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
@@ -275,7 +275,7 @@
 	if (protocol < 0 || protocol >= IPPROTO_MAX)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (!current_has_network())
+	if (!kern && !current_has_network())
 		return -EACCES;
 
 	sock->state = SS_UNCONNECTED;
--- a/net/ipv6/af_inet6.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/af_inet6.c
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@
 	if (protocol < 0 || protocol >= IPPROTO_MAX)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (!current_has_network())
+	if (!kern && !current_has_network())
 		return -EACCES;
 
 	/* Look for the requested type/protocol pair. */
